# L §3.3: rate ± rate only "of one period"; comparisons "within one period".  A yearly and a monthly rate
# added are refused ("rate arithmetic outside §3.3"); the periods are in the values, so this is found when the
# values are read: tally 2.1.7 (R5, issue #144; P66 reopened), a check whose input only the run knows prints
# RUN-DOMAIN at the value with load's words (L §8.4); 2.1.6 printed LOAD-UNIT for the whole reality.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01
unit hour "godzina"

input a: rate
input b: rate

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = 5 %/year
  b = 0.5 %/month

ask q1: a + b
=== expect
q1: refused: RUN-DOMAIN rates of different periods: 0.05 /year + 0.005 /month
  cut 2026-01-01
